we could shift to B if we think stress handling outweighs communication issues. But we need to be evidence-based.\n\nLet's respond: I agree with Sarah on C's reliability and crew atmosphere, but note that his egocentric and communication difficulty could impair cockpit coordination, which is critical. Compare with B's stress handling but his nasty remarks raise similar concerns. D's hot temper also problematic. A's leadership but show-off and not open to new ideas may hinder adaptability. Therefore I still recommend C, but we need to probe his communication style further.\n\nThus we state vote for Candidate C.\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: \"100% reliable\", \"creates a positive crew atmosphere\", \"difficulty communicating ideas\", \"egocentric\", \"not willing to further education\". Also mention B's \"handles stress very well\" and \"makes nasty remarks\". And D's \"hot temper\". Provide reasoning.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
